<title>HONG KONG: HK observatory reports quake east of Philippines.</title>
<headline>HK observatory reports quake east of Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake was detected east of the Philippines on Monday, the Royal Hong Kong Observatory said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The observatory said the quake, recorded at 2057 local time (1257 GMT Monday), was located about 360 kilometres (225 miles) east of Cebu and was estimated at 5.5 on the Richter scale .</p>
